      "hints": [
        "Expand $(1 + 2x)^5$ up to the term in $x^2$ using the binomial theorem $\\binom{5}{r}(1)^{5-r}(2x)^r$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Apply the binomial theorem to expand $(1 + 2x)^5$ in ascending powers of $x$:\n$$(1 + 2x)^5 = \\binom{5}{0}(1)^5 + \\binom{5}{1}(1)^4(2x) + \\binom{5}{2}(1)^3(2x)^2 + \\dots$$",
        "Calculate each coefficient and simplify:\n$$= 1 + 5(2x) + 10(4x^2) = 1 + 10x + 40x^2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
